A `Channel` cannot be bound, stored, returned or compared here: a channel is used only as the receiver of `send`, the iterable of a `for...of`, an argument, or a field its class's constructor sets from a parameter, so it is never bound, stored, returned or captured, and which tasks reach it is a question the checker can answer; hand it to the task as its argument, `s.spawn(task, ch)`, or as a field the argument's constructor sets, `s.spawn(task, new Work(ch, n))`
